{"result": {"id": "chatcmpl-2ce4bc9eb107465d81890de081ac057e", "choices": [{"finish_reason": "stop", "index": 0, "logprobs": null, "message": {"content": "{\n    \"title\": \"SAP Technology Overview as of 2025\",\n    \"summary\": \"This report provides an overview of SAP's key technology components, highlighting their relationships and significant updates as of 2025. The information is relevant to SAP's technology operations and development processes.\",\n    \"rating\": 9.5,\n    \"rating_explanation\": \"The high importance rating reflects the critical roles that SAP's technology components play in supporting the company's operations, development, and innovation efforts.\",\n    \"findings\": [\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Cloud Foundry Environment Updates\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The Cloud Foundry environment has seen significant updates in 2025, including the addition of new regions, enhancements to the Create Node dialog, and improvements to the landscape action logs. These updates aim to simplify navigation, enhance automation, and provide more flexible table layouts for better data management. [Data: Sources (961, 962, 963), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 06), (2025, 08, 14))]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"API Gateway Module Updates\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The API Gateway module has undergone several updates in 2025, including the introduction of APIRule v2, the upgrade to version 3.0.2, and the update to version 3.1.3. These updates aim to provide more flexible access strategies, improve in-cluster connectivity, and enhance the overall API management experience. [Data: Sources (964, 965, 304), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 05), (2025, 08, 13))]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Data Space Integration Updates\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Data Space Integration has seen several updates in 2025, including the introduction of new features such as Assignees Column, Software Version Update, and Contract References. These updates aim to provide more efficient data management, enhance collaboration, and improve overall data integration. [Data: Sources (966, 967, 1454), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 04), (2025, 02, 08))]\"\n        }\n    ],\n    \"date_range\": [\"2025-01-01\", \"2025-08-14\"]\n}", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "annotations": null, "audio": null, "function_call": null, "tool_calls": [], "reasoning_content": null}, "stop_reason": null, "token_ids": null}], "created": 1758948413, "model": "unsloth/Meta-Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct", "object": "chat.completion", "service_tier": null, "system_fingerprint": null, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 481, "prompt_tokens": 8888, "total_tokens": 9369, "completion_tokens_details": null, "prompt_tokens_details": null}, "prompt_logprobs": null, "prompt_token_ids": null, "kv_transfer_params": null}, "input": {"messages": [{"content": "\nYou are an AI assistant that helps a human analyst to perform general information discovery.\nInformation discovery is the process of identifying and assessing relevant information associated with certain entities (e.g., organizations and individuals) within a network.\n\n# Goal\nWrite a comprehensive report of a community, given a list of entities that belong to the community as well as their relationships and optional associated claims.\nThe report will be used to inform decision-makers about information associated with the community and their potential impact.\nThe content of this report includes an overview of the community's key entities, their core attributes or capabilities, their connections, and noteworthy claims.\nRetain as much time specific information as possible so your end user can build a timeline of events.\n\n# Report Structure\nThe report should include the following sections:\n- TITLE: community's name that represents its key entities - title should be short but specific. When possible, include representative named entities in the title. Avoid including phrases like 'eligibility assessment' or 'eligibility assessment report' in the title.\n- SUMMARY: An executive summary of the community's overall structure, how its entities are related to each other, and significant program-specific or eligibility-related insights.\n- IMPORTANCE RATING: A float score between 0-10 that represents the importance of entities within the community..\n- RATING EXPLANATION: Give a single sentence explanation of the importance rating.\n- DETAILED FINDINGS: A list of 5-10 key insights about the community. Each insight should have a short summary followed by multiple paragraphs of explanatory text grounded according to the grounding rules below. Be comprehensive.\n- DATE RANGE: A range of dates (YYYY-MM-DD) with the format [START, END] which corresponds to the date range of text units and intermediate reports used to build the report.\n\nReturn output as a well-formed JSON-formatted string with the following format. Don't use any unnecessary escape sequences. The output should be a single JSON object that can be parsed by json.loads.\n    {\n        \"title\": \"<report_title>\",\n        \"summary\": \"<executive_summary>\",\n        \"rating\": <importance_rating>,\n        \"rating_explanation\": \"<rating_explanation>\",\n        \"findings\": [{\"summary\":\"<insight_1_summary>\", \"explanation\": \"<insight_1_explanation\"}, {\"summary\":\"<insight_2_summary>\", \"explanation\": \"<insight_2_explanation\"}],\n\t\t\"date_range\": [\"<date range start>\", \"<date range end>\"],\n\n    }\n\n# Grounding Rules\nPoints supported by data should list their data references as follows:\n\n\"This is an example sentence supported by multiple data references [Data: <dataset name> (record ids), <dataset name> (record ids)].\"\n\nDo not list more than 5 record ids in a single reference. Instead, list the top 5 most relevant record ids and add \"+more\" to indicate that there are more.\n\nFor example:\n\"Person X resolved a major issue with project Y [Data: Sources (1, 5),  Date_Range ((2001, 05, 12), (2001, 05, 14))]. He also made major updates to the database of app Y [Data: Reports (2, 4), Sources (7, 23, 2, 34, 46, +more), Date_Range ((2001, 05, 15), (2001, 05, 18))\"\"\n\nwhere 1, 2, 4, 5, 7, 23, 2, 34, and 46 represent the id (not the index) of the relevant data record.\n\nLimit the total report length to 2000 words.\n\n# Example Input\n-----------\nSOURCES\nid, text\n1, Text: From: compliance.office@enron.com To: management.team@enron.com Cc: legal.team@enron.com, risk@enron.com Date: Wed, 12 Jul 2000 08:30:00 -0600 (CST) Subject: Quick Update on Compliance & Risk Efforts\n2, Quick update on what's been cooking in Compliance and Risk Management. Risk Management is stepping up — They've been tightening up on our financial risk assessments and mitigation strategies since early this year.\n3, Their efforts are key to keeping us on solid ground financially and in compliance with the latest market regulations as of mid-2000. It's crucial for our strategic planning and helps us stay ahead.\n5, Legal's keeping us in check — The Legal Compliance team is on top of ensuring all our operations are up to scratch with legal standards. They're especially focused on improving our corporate governance and contract management as of the second quarter of 2000. This is critical for keeping our operations smooth and legally sound.\n9, Working together — Risk Management and Legal Compliance have been syncing up better than ever since the start of Q2 2000. They're making sure our strategies are not just effective but also fully compliant. This coordination is essential for our integrated governance approach.\n10, Your thoughts? — How do these updates impact your area? Got ideas on how we can do better? Give your department heads a shout.\n11, Thanks for staying engaged. Let's keep pushing for better and smarter ways to work. Cheers, Jane Doe\n\nOutput:\n\n{\n    \"title\": \"Enron Compliance and Risk Management Overview as of July 2000\",\n    \"summary\": \"This report delves into Enron's key departments focusing on compliance and risk management, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to uphold regulatory standards and manage financial risks effectively. The information is relevant to the company's operations around mid-2000.\",\n    \"rating\": 9.2,\n    \"rating_explanation\": \"The high importance rating reflects the critical roles that the Risk Management and Legal Compliance Departments play in ensuring Enron's adherence to financial and legal regulations, crucial for maintaining the company's integrity and operational stability.\",\n    \"findings\": [\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Risk Management Operational Scope\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The Risk Management Department at Enron plays a pivotal role in identifying, assessing, and mitigating financial risks. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2000, helps safeguard Enron against potential financial pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective risk management not only prevents financial anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes.\n\n[Data: Sources (2, 3), Date_Range ((2000, 01, 01), (2000, 07, 12))]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Legal Compliance and Governance\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The Legal Compliance Department ensures that all Enron's operations adhere to the legal standards set by regulatory bodies. Their focus on corporate governance and contract management, noted starting Q2 2000, is crucial in maintaining Enron's reputation and operational legality, especially in managing complex contracts and corporate agreements. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high legal standards and ethical practices.\n\n[Data: Source (5), Date_Range ((2000, 04, 01), (2000, 07, 12))]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Interdepartmental Collaboration for Compliance\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Collaboration between the Risk Management and Legal Compliance Departments, established in Q2 2000, ensures that risk mitigation strategies are legally sound and that compliance measures consider financial risks. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating risk management with legal compliance strategies at Enron. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with regulatory requirements.\n\n[Data: Sources (9), Date_Range ((2000, 04, 01), (2000, 07, 12))]\"\n        }\n    ],\n    \"date_range\": [\"2000-01-01\", \"2000-07-12\"]\n}\n\n\n# Real Data\n\nUse the following text for your answer. Do not make anything up in your answer.\n\nText:\n-----SOURCES-----\nid,text,entity_degree\n346,\"--- Record 1061 ---\nComponent: Data Space Integration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Operator \"\"Exists\"\" for Company Policies\nDescription: When you create rules for company policies, you can now use the operator exists in combination with the attribute contract reference. Create a new rule, select the attribute contract reference, then select exists. The value of the rule is left empty on purpose to define that the company policy should check if any contract reference exists in the provider's offer.  See Create and Edit Company Policies.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-04-10\nValid as Of: 2025-04-10\nVersion: 2502\n\n--- Record 1062 ---\nComponent: Data Space Integration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Software Version Update\nDescription: The following are the latest versions in Data Space Integration:      Data Space Integration: 1.7.*      Increment: 2502      Tractus-X Eclipse Dataspace Connector: 0.7.6      FOSS Eclipse Dataspace Components: 0.7.2      See also the Release Notes of Catena-X. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-04-10\nValid as Of: 2025-04-10\nVersion: 2502\n\n--- Record 1063 ---\nComponent: Mobile Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Access: BTP Cockpit & Dev Space Manager\nDescription: (Version 2503) To simplify navigation to your SAP BTP Cockpit and Dev Space Manager, we have added direct links in the Mobile Services cockpit.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-04-10\nValid as Of: 2025-04-10\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1064 ---\nComponent: Mobile Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Full Initial Download from Offline Service\nDescription: (Version 2503) We've introduced a new feature labeled as Trigger Initial Download, this feature lets you initiate the full download of app data from the offline service and cancel the full initial download if needed. You can trigger this download from application level also registration level.For more information, see Managing App Users and Device Registrations and Defining Offline Settings for Applications.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-04-10\nValid as Of: 2025-04-10\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1065 ---\nComponent: Mobile Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Include Predefined Annotations\nDescription: (Version 2503) We've introduced a new checkbox to enable predefined annotations for sample OData for testing.  For more information, see Using the Sample ODATA ESPM\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-04-10\nValid as Of: 2025-04-10\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1066 ---\nComponent: Mobile Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Update: Logout Service\nDescription: (Version 2503) When the Logout API is called, it removes registrations for registered users and devices related with the push feature from the server.  For more information, see DELETE User Logout Request and POST User Logout Request.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-04-10\nValid as Of: 2025-04-10\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1067 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: API Gateway module: Update to version 2.11.3\nDescription: We have implemented a watch mechanism to ensure that DNSEntry is up to date with the IP and host of the istio-ingressgateway service. Additionally, we've decreased the default reconciliation time to safeguard against possible scheduling errors.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-04-09\nValid as Of: 2025-04-09\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1068 ---\nComponent: SAP Task Center\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Feedback Option for Documentation\nDescription: You can now provide feedback on the SAP Task Center documentation using the Feedback  Comments function on the SAP Help Portal, without the need to use GitHub. You just need to log in to the SAP Help Portal with your email.   For more information, see Creating Better Documentation Together: SAP Help Portal’s new approach to Collaboration and Feedback.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-04-09\nValid as Of: 2025-04-09\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1069 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Identity Authentication (using SCIM API version 2) - changed behavior\nDescription: Similar to the Local Identity Directory, you can now use Identity Authentication (SCIM API version 2) for reading and writing application-specific groups. Depending on the configured pair of provisioning systems, to ensure successful provisioning, you might need to manually define value mappings for the attribute applicationId in the source or the target system transformations.  For more information, see:    Identity Authentication (Source)  Identity Authentication (Target)  List of Properties→ips.application.id  \nAction: Info only\",3202\n429,\"--- Record 961 ---\nComponent: Cloud Transport Management\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Enhancements to the Create Node dialog.\nDescription: When you create or edit a transport node, the destination selection box now displays both the name and description of each destination. The description makes it easier to choose the appropriate destination.  See:   Create Transport Nodes  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Application Development and Integration\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-06\nValid as Of: 2025-05-06\nVersion: 2504a\n\n--- Record 962 ---\nComponent: Cloud Transport Management\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New function in the import queue: Immediately start imports of transport requests as soon as they enter an import queue.\nDescription: This function enhances automation, and simplifies the import process.  See:   Enable Automatic Import  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Application Development and Integration\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-06\nValid as Of: 2025-05-06\nVersion: 2504a\n\n--- Record 963 ---\nComponent: Cloud Transport Management\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Revamp of the Landscape Action Logs\nDescription: The landscape action logs are now displayed in a more flexible table layout with extensive filter options, detail display, and links to the affected objects.   See:   Landscape Action Logs  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Application Development and Integration\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-06\nValid as Of: 2025-05-06\nVersion: 2504a\n\n--- Record 964 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: API Gateway module: APIRule v2 upgrade and deletion of v1beta1 are postponed\nDescription:     After careful consideration, we have decided to postpone the release of API Gateway 3.0.0, which contains the APIRule v2 upgrade, to May 5, 2025.  Additionally, the planned deletion of v1beta1 for the end of May will also be postponed. A new target date will be announced in the future.  Required action: Migrate all your APIRule custom resources (CRs) to version v2.      To migrate your APIRule CRs from version v2alpha1 to version v2, you must update the version in APIRule CRs’ metadata.  To migrate your APIRule CRs from version v1beta1 to v2, follow the procedure described in the blog posts:   APIRule migration - noAuth and jwt handlers  APIRule migration - Ory Oathkeeper based OAuth2 handlers    For more information, see Changes Introduced in APIRule v2alpha1 and v2. Since the APIRule CRD v2alpha1 is identical to v2, the migration procedure from version v1beta1 to version v2 is the same as from version v1beta1 to version v2alpha1.\nAction: Required\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-04-16\nValid as Of: 2025-05-05\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 965 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: API Gateway module: Update to version 3.0.2\nDescription: This version of the API Gateway module introduces APIRule CR in the stable version v2.   The new CRD allows you to expose your workloads using one of the three supported access strategies: jwt, noAuth, and extAuth. The noAuth access strategy provides a simple configuration for exposing workloads over the specified HTTP methods. The jwt access strategy allows you to secure your workload by defining Istio JWT configuration and the extAuth access strategy allows for providing custom authentication and authorization logic. For more information, see APIRule Custom Resource.  Additionally, version 3.0.2 contains the following fixes:  We've fixed the behavior of in-cluster connectivity when using JWT handler in APIRule. Now, in-cluster connectivity is blocked.  Now, when you create an APIRule with the noAuth access strategy, it is validated if the target workload has an Istio sidecar proxy injected.  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-05\nValid as Of: 2025-05-05\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 966 ---\nComponent: Data Space Integration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Assignees Column Available in Company Policies\nDescription: In the list of company policies (Configure  Data Spaces), the column Assignees now shows you how many clients are already assigned to the company policy.  See Create and Edit Company Policies.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-04\nValid as Of: 2025-05-04\nVersion: 2503\n\n--- Record 967 ---\nComponent: Data Space Integration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Software Version Update\nDescription: The following are the latest versions in Data Space Integration:      Data Space Integration: 1.8.*      Increment: 2503      Tractus-X Eclipse Dataspace Connector: 0.7.6      FOSS Eclipse Dataspace Components: 0.7.2      See also the Release Notes of Catena-X. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-04\nValid as Of: \",3202\n329,\"--- Record 1251 ---\nComponent: Integration Advisor\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Neo\nTitle: Software Version Update\nDescription:   SAP Integration Advisor: 1.97.*    Increment: 2501    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-11\nValid as Of: 2025-03-11\nVersion: 2501\n\n--- Record 1252 ---\nComponent: SAP Task Center\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Boosters Set Up SAP Task Center with the all-tasks Service Plan\nDescription: The SAP Task Center boosters have been updated to set up SAP Task Center with the all-tasks service plan.   For more information on the service plans, see Service Plans and Metering.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-11\nValid as Of: 2025-03-11\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1253 ---\nComponent: UI Theme Designer\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Neo\nTitle: Theming Base Content for CF and Neo.\nDescription: The base theming content is updated to version 11.27.1. Review the changes at https://github.com/SAP/theming-base-content/releases.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2025-03-11\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1254 ---\nComponent: SAP Business Application Studio\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Development Experience\nDescription: You can now use the Runtime Capabilities editor to add Audit Logging to your full stack project. See Runtime Capabilities Editor.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-10\nValid as Of: 2025-03-10\nVersion: T2502a\n\n--- Record 1255 ---\nComponent: SAP Business Application Studio\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Development Experience\nDescription: When creating a new MDK project, you can now use capital letters in the project name.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-10\nValid as Of: 2025-03-10\nVersion: T2502a\n\n--- Record 1256 ---\nComponent: SAP Business Application Studio\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Development Experience\nDescription: You can now run your CAP Java application using a run configuration and configure how you want to run with remote OData services. See Creating Run Configurations for Java CAP Applications..\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-10\nValid as Of: 2025-03-10\nVersion: T2502a\n\n--- Record 1257 ---\nComponent: API Management\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Supported AsyncAPI Versions\nDescription: You can now import events more efficiently with enhanced support for AsyncAPI versions 2.5.0 and 2.6.0. For more information, see Import Events as AsyncAPI on Developer Hub.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-09\nValid as Of: 2025-03-09\nVersion: 2501\n\n--- Record 1258 ---\nComponent: Data Space Integration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Consuming Azure Assets\nDescription: You can now consume assets of type Azure. Before you can consume Azure assets, you must create credentials using your Azure account.   For more details and Azure-specific payload examples, see Consuming S3 and Azure Assets and the Transfer Process API on SAP Business Accelerator Hub.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-09\nValid as Of: 2025-03-09\nVersion: 2501\n\n--- Record 1259 ---\nComponent: Data Space Integration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Software Version Update\nDescription: The following are the latest versions in Data Space Integration:      Data Space Integration: 1.6.*      Increment: 2501      Tractus-X Eclipse Dataspace Connector: 0.7.6      FOSS Eclipse Dataspace Components: 0.7.2      See also the Release Notes of Catena-X. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-09\nValid as Of: 2025-03-09\nVersion: 2501\n\n--- Record 1260 ---\nComponent: Edge Integration Cell\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Additional Request Reply Step for API Artifact\nDescription: You can now add multiple request-reply steps to an API artifact, allowing for seamless integration with multiple target endpoints or service callouts.  See: Creating Additional Request Reply Step for API Artifact\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-09\nValid as Of: 2025-03-09\nVersion: 2501\n\n\",2595\n706,\"--- Record 301 ---\nComponent: SAP Task Center\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Feature  Activity Log\nDescription: You can now view your task's history with the Activity Log in the SAP Task Center Web app.  For more information, see Activity Log, Attachments and Comments.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-14\nValid as Of: 2025-08-14\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 302 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Delivering an Add-On Product with the Landscape Portal\nDescription: If you have an SAP Partner Edge Build contract, you can now publish a product as an add-on product. This offers a second delivery option for partners as an alternative to the multitenancy SaaS solution. Your product will appear in the SAP Store, where eligible customers can install it in their own SAP BTP ABAP environment system. The Landscape Portal is used for both, to publish add-on products by partners, and to install them by the customers.  For more information, see New Software Delivery Option \"\"Add-On Product\"\".\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-12\nValid as Of: 2025-08-13\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2508\n\n--- Record 303 ---\nComponent: Cloud Integration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: IBM MQ Adapter Supports New Version\nDescription: A new version 1.3.0 of the IBM MQ adapter supports Client Certificate based authentication for JMS Variants.  See: IBM MQ Adapter\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-13\nValid as Of: 2025-08-13\nVersion: 2506\n\n--- Record 304 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: API Gateway module: Update to version 3.1.3\nDescription: The new version brings the following changes:      Now, APIRules v1beta1 that are not migrated to version v2 are in the Warning state.    In the controller, the deployed images are now provided using environment variables.  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-12\nValid as Of: 2025-08-13\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 305 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Production - Document Pricing – Do Not Lose Condition Values During Repricing\nDescription: If a price recalculation with type C (Carries out a new pricing, manually entered conditions are retained) was triggered, an automatically determined condition value used to get lost in the following case: The condition appeared twice in the results, one value with control flag A (Adjust for quantity variance) and origin flag A (Automatic pricing) and another value with control flag C (Changed manually) and origin flag C (Manually entered/changed). This issue has been corrected, which can lead to unexpected pricing results if the issue was unnoticed before.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-25\nValid as Of: 2025-08-13\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 306 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Production - Support More Standard Pricing Routines\nDescription: There are some newly supported pricing requirement formulas:    11 No Material    20 Price Charge    28 No Variant (SA)    29 No Exception 'N'  30 No Exclusion 'V'  35 Plant Info Record  37 Variant  42 Pricing – Normal  57 Not Free Goods w/o return item    Newly supported pricing base value formulas:  23 Preference  25 Cash Discount  44 VAT France  61 Preference  220 Gross Value    See: Supported Standard Pricing Exits.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-25\nValid as Of: 2025-08-13\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 307 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Production – Size Limit for Price Determination Trace\nDescription: Pricing service will stop writing pricing determination traces when an estimated memory size of about 5MB was reached. That should be sufficient for most cases. When the limit is reached, a corresponding info message is added to the trace. SAP can optimize this size limit for support cases and can furthermore limit the pricing determination trace to a list of relevant condition types.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-25\nValid as Of: 2025-08-13\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 308 ---\nComponent: Responsibility Management Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Data Center\nDescription: The Responsibility Management Service is now also available on the Google Cloud Platform in AP30 (Sydney, Australia). See Pricing and Regions Information.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-13\nValid as Of: 2025-08-13\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 309 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Integration with Document Grounding\nDescription: The document grounding capability uses information gathered from documents\",2595\n336,\"--- Record 1451 ---\nComponent: SAP Business Application Studio\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Development Experience\nDescription: The Project Overview is now available for CAP projects. See Project Overview.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-09\nValid as Of: 2025-02-09\nVersion: T2501a\n\n--- Record 1452 ---\nComponent: API Management\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitl